1
00:01:50,413 --> 00:01:52,148
So late! Way too late!

2
00:01:52,582 --> 00:01:54,751
Oh, Terai-san hasn't arrived yet?

3
00:01:55,251 --> 00:02:00,189
We're supposed to arrive ten minutes before the handover. What is he doing?

4
00:02:00,523 --> 00:02:04,227
I can't wait any longer. I'm gonna go eat!

5
00:02:05,061 --> 00:02:08,231
Hey, your shift doesn't finish for another five minutes!

6
00:02:08,431 --> 00:02:09,766
Don't be so picky!

7
00:02:09,999 --> 00:02:11,567
Sorry to be late.

8
00:02:16,773 --> 00:02:18,875
Sorry, but who are you again?

9
00:02:19,308 --> 00:02:21,611
It's me, Terai.

10
00:02:21,844 --> 00:02:24,447
Eh! No way!

11
00:02:25,948 --> 00:02:28,317
Don't act so surprised.

12
00:02:29,652 --> 00:02:31,721
His voice does sound like Terai-san, but...

13
00:02:31,921 --> 00:02:33,122
Don't be silly!

14
00:02:33,322 --> 00:02:37,927
Terai's body and face are round like a steamed bun.

15
00:02:38,394 --> 00:02:40,229
Even if you say that...

16
00:02:40,463 --> 00:02:44,801
If you're Terai, you would always carry photos of your family with you.

17
00:02:45,034 --> 00:02:46,102
Okay...

18
00:02:46,302 --> 00:02:48,204
It's true. This is Terai's family.

19
00:02:48,604 --> 00:02:51,941
See? We take photos together once a week.

20
00:02:52,141 --> 00:02:53,943
Reiko, give me those.

21
00:02:57,280 --> 00:03:01,451
I see. This way, we can see this man used to be Terai.

22
00:03:01,651 --> 00:03:02,952
What happened, Terai-san?

23
00:03:03,152 --> 00:03:05,455
Commuting is a little bit tough.

24
00:03:05,655 --> 00:03:09,692
Oh, you did say you'd bought a house. How long is your commute?

25
00:03:09,926 --> 00:03:11,961
About a seven-hour round trip.

26
00:03:12,161 --> 00:03:13,229
Seven hours!

27
00:03:13,796 --> 00:03:19,001
The chief has a five-hour round trip. So, that's two hours longer than him!

28
00:03:19,435 --> 00:03:24,006
When I try to buy a house with my income, there's no other way.

29
00:03:24,807 --> 00:03:27,443
I usually get up before dawn.

30
00:03:27,643 --> 00:03:30,079
I don't want to wake up the whole family,

31
00:03:30,279 --> 00:03:33,249
so I have a simple meal of leftovers from the night before.

32
00:03:33,449 --> 00:03:35,318
It takes one hour by bicycle to the station.

33
00:03:35,952 --> 00:03:38,855
I finally arrive at the station at dawn,

34
00:03:40,256 --> 00:03:42,458
and the train is always packed.

35
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:49,532
I have to change trains five times, and if I miss one, I'm late.

36
00:03:49,732 --> 00:03:51,167
I'm desperate.

37
00:03:54,871 --> 00:03:57,006
Kameari, Kameari.

38
00:03:58,040 --> 00:04:00,376
Then it's the same on the way back home.

39
00:04:00,576 --> 00:04:01,577
What a tragic fate.

40
00:04:01,811 --> 00:04:03,379
You'll break down someday.

41
00:04:03,713 --> 00:04:06,716
But owning a home is a salaryman's dream.

42
00:04:06,949 --> 00:04:07,884
Some sacrifice is...

43
00:04:08,117 --> 00:04:09,519
Watch out!

44
00:04:09,719 --> 00:04:10,586
I'm sorry.

45
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:13,656
Why don't you at least try to eat something nutritious?

46
00:04:13,856 --> 00:04:15,658
Your body won't last like this.

47
00:04:15,858 --> 00:04:18,127
Yeah! I was just about to go out to eat.

48
00:04:18,327 --> 00:04:22,198
Let's go eat something that will give us stamina, like yakiniku or suppon turtle!

49
00:04:22,398 --> 00:04:25,902
You're not trying to get Terai-san to treat you, are you, Ryo-chan?

50
00:04:26,135 --> 00:04:27,136
Yikes!

51
00:04:28,204 --> 00:04:31,707
I don't have the money for such an expensive meal.

52
00:04:31,908 --> 00:04:34,977
I've decided to spend 350 yen a day on food.

53
00:04:35,178 --> 00:04:36,612
350 yen?!

54
00:04:36,846 --> 00:04:40,082
You could only buy bread and milk at best.

55
00:04:40,316 --> 00:04:42,151
Yes, I have that often.

56
00:04:42,351 --> 00:04:45,254
-350 yen is enough! -Huh?

57
00:04:45,788 --> 00:04:51,160
With just 350 yen, I'll stuff you full of something tasty, Terai!

58
00:04:57,733 --> 00:04:58,734
Welcome!

59
00:04:58,935 --> 00:05:01,337
Ryo-san, what do you want today?

60
00:05:01,537 --> 00:05:03,606
You're obviously lacking vitamins.

61
00:05:03,806 --> 00:05:05,741
You need to eat plenty of fruit.

62
00:05:05,942 --> 00:05:07,476
"350 YEN FOR ONE PILE"

63
00:05:07,643 --> 00:05:08,477
Apples...

64
00:05:08,945 --> 00:05:11,547
350 yen will blow the whole budget!

65
00:05:11,747 --> 00:05:14,650
Fresh apples, just arrived from the farm today.

66
00:05:14,884 --> 00:05:16,752
Sweet, fresh, and full of flavor!

67
00:05:18,721 --> 00:05:22,758
For something just arrived today, there's too much dust on the stem.

68
00:05:22,959 --> 00:05:26,729
It must have been in the store for at least three days!

69
00:05:26,929 --> 00:05:27,630
Gulp!

70
00:05:27,830 --> 00:05:28,931
Make it 200 yen!

71
00:05:29,131 --> 00:05:33,035
You got me, Ryo-san. Fine, 200 yen.

72
00:05:33,236 --> 00:05:35,638
The bottom part is pretty damaged.

73
00:05:35,838 --> 00:05:37,573
This is 100 yen.

74
00:05:37,773 --> 00:05:39,976
All right, 100 yen is fine.

75
00:05:40,209 --> 00:05:42,845
Looking closely, there are traces of insect bites.

76
00:05:43,079 --> 00:05:44,146
50 yen!

77
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:45,581
Yes, that's fine.

78
00:05:46,115 --> 00:05:47,950
I can push one more time.

79
00:05:49,919 --> 00:05:52,321
What's this apple? It's hollow inside!

80
00:05:52,521 --> 00:05:54,624
K-Keep your voice down, Ryo-san!

81
00:05:54,824 --> 00:05:57,326
Are you trying to sell these hollow apples

82
00:05:57,526 --> 00:06:00,696
to the housewives of Katsushika?

83
00:06:00,930 --> 00:06:02,965
What a terrible store. I didn't know.

84
00:06:03,165 --> 00:06:06,235
Okay, okay, you can take a whole pile for 10 yen!

85
00:06:06,435 --> 00:06:10,239
Oh, why didn't you just say so? I'll take it then.

86
00:06:11,107 --> 00:06:14,677
No, no! Even at 500 yen, this is a crazy bargain.

87
00:06:14,877 --> 00:06:16,512
Not a single yen less!

88
00:06:16,979 --> 00:06:19,148
He's such a stubborn guy.

89
00:06:19,515 --> 00:06:20,449
Oh, I know!

90
00:06:20,650 --> 00:06:24,487
Well, weren't you in front of the off-track betting place last Sunday?

91
00:06:24,687 --> 00:06:25,321
Gulp!

92
00:06:25,521 --> 00:06:28,658
Your wife banned you from gambling, didn't she?

93
00:06:28,858 --> 00:06:30,493
W-What are you talking about?

94
00:06:30,693 --> 00:06:32,295
Oh, playing dumb, huh?

95
00:06:32,495 --> 00:06:35,031
Ma'am! Let me tell you something!

96
00:06:38,968 --> 00:06:40,803
Hey! Why is the baby crying?

97
00:06:41,270 --> 00:06:42,805
Don't cry! Look!

98
00:06:43,005 --> 00:06:46,876
Peek-a-boo! Blah blah blah!

99
00:06:48,511 --> 00:06:50,112
Come on, Ryo-san, give me a break.

100
00:06:50,312 --> 00:06:53,749
My wife just came back from her parents' house.

101
00:06:53,983 --> 00:06:56,485
Oh, that's great.

102
00:06:56,686 --> 00:06:58,354
So, how much is this?

103
00:06:58,554 --> 00:07:01,691
I have no choice. I'll make it 300 yen.

104
00:07:02,758 --> 00:07:04,860
Ma'am! Guess what!

105
00:07:05,061 --> 00:07:07,763
50 yen, no, 30 yen will be fine!

106
00:07:12,201 --> 00:07:13,369
Here, take it, you thief!

107
00:07:13,569 --> 00:07:15,304
Fine, I'll take it.

108
00:07:16,205 --> 00:07:16,906
Thank you...

109
00:07:17,139 --> 00:07:19,008
Ryo-san, you're amazing.

110
00:07:23,846 --> 00:07:25,881
I'm stuffed!

111
00:07:26,348 --> 00:07:28,250
I'm full too.

112
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:34,490
I never thought I could eat this much for just 350 yen.

113
00:07:34,924 --> 00:07:37,960
We ate it together, so the price was half that!

114
00:07:38,627 --> 00:07:40,363
It's all thanks to Ryo-san.

115
00:07:40,563 --> 00:07:43,399
You're a genius when it comes to bargaining!

116
00:07:43,599 --> 00:07:45,101
Call me the King of Shopping.

117
00:07:45,334 --> 00:07:47,703
There's nothing I can't knock the price down on!

118
00:07:47,903 --> 00:07:51,273
When you buy a new house, come to me, Terai.

119
00:07:51,507 --> 00:07:54,977
You bought your current house after consulting with Chief Ohara, right?

120
00:07:55,444 --> 00:07:59,281
Yeah, he is the one who knows a lot about real estate in Katsushika PD

121
00:07:59,515 --> 00:08:01,951
They say he's a real estate demon.

122
00:08:02,384 --> 00:08:03,452
A real estate demon?

123
00:08:03,652 --> 00:08:06,789
"REAL ESTATE"

124
00:08:07,456 --> 00:08:09,792
Hmph! And now you have a seven-hour commute!

125
00:08:09,992 --> 00:08:12,928
It was a mistake to ask the chief for advice in the first place.

126
00:08:13,129 --> 00:08:16,198
He can't even buy a single radish properly by himself.

127
00:08:16,399 --> 00:08:19,301
How could someone like that possibly buy a house?

128
00:08:20,636 --> 00:08:21,971
Let's get back to work.

129
00:08:22,204 --> 00:08:23,939
I'll look for that document...

130
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:27,009
Hey, what's wrong with you two?

131
00:08:34,583 --> 00:08:36,585
Ch-Chief, I didn't know you were here!

132
00:08:37,119 --> 00:08:39,989
You were talking pretty big, weren't you?

133
00:08:40,222 --> 00:08:43,592
Well, I was just giving my opinion as a shopping pro.

134
00:08:44,026 --> 00:08:45,761
A shopping pro?

135
00:08:46,462 --> 00:08:50,032
Buying and selling real estate is different from regular shopping.

136
00:08:50,266 --> 00:08:52,568
It's not as easy as you think!

137
00:08:53,002 --> 00:08:56,038
Why? You pay money, you get stuff. Same thing!

138
00:08:57,406 --> 00:09:01,577
Okay then, do you fully understand the Real Property Registration Act?

139
00:09:03,045 --> 00:09:05,881
Good luck, birdbrain!

140
00:09:06,449 --> 00:09:08,818
Do you know what "building coverage ratio" means?

141
00:09:09,018 --> 00:09:12,288
For large contracts, you also need knowledge of civil law.

142
00:09:12,488 --> 00:09:13,656
Th-That's...

143
00:09:13,856 --> 00:09:17,793
What about the Building Standards Act and the Real Estate Brokerage Act?

144
00:09:21,730 --> 00:09:25,067
"BUILDING STANDARDS ACT"

145
00:09:25,301 --> 00:09:31,073
"REAL ESTATE BROKERAGE ACT"

146
00:09:31,874 --> 00:09:34,376
What about the Land Lease Act and the Building Lease Act?

147
00:09:34,610 --> 00:09:37,480
The Act on Building Unit Ownership, etc.?

148
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:40,015
The Act on Provisional Registration Secured Claims?

149
00:09:40,216 --> 00:09:43,919
The Constitution, the Commercial Code, the Penal Code, and the Road Traffic Act?

150
00:09:52,528 --> 00:09:56,232
You gotta be kidding! I don't need such useless legal knowledge!

151
00:09:56,699 --> 00:09:57,900
How dare you say "useless"?

152
00:09:58,100 --> 00:10:00,236
What would you know? You've never bought a house!

153
00:10:00,769 --> 00:10:01,637
I know plenty!

154
00:10:01,837 --> 00:10:04,874
Besides, you live on the edge of Chiba!

155
00:10:05,074 --> 00:10:07,243
I chose my house for its environment!

156
00:10:07,743 --> 00:10:10,079
So, is Terai's house also for the environment?

157
00:10:10,312 --> 00:10:12,548
There weren't any better places!

158
00:10:12,748 --> 00:10:14,383
You're just bad at searching!

159
00:10:14,583 --> 00:10:16,752
Then, you think you can find a better one?

160
00:10:16,952 --> 00:10:20,489
I'll find a house that's better than yours and more convenient to commute.

161
00:10:20,689 --> 00:10:21,657
Interesting!

162
00:10:21,857 --> 00:10:25,261
Then in one week, you'll take me to the house you find.

163
00:10:25,761 --> 00:10:26,896
Bring it on!

164
00:10:27,096 --> 00:10:28,764
What if you can't find one?

165
00:10:29,198 --> 00:10:31,767
I'll go around Tokyo naked!

166
00:10:31,967 --> 00:10:32,968
What?

167
00:10:33,369 --> 00:10:35,371
The deadline is one week from now! Got it?

168
00:10:35,571 --> 00:10:36,438
Fine!

169
00:10:49,818 --> 00:10:52,888
Ryo-san, are you sure about making a promise like that?

170
00:10:53,088 --> 00:10:55,791
I'd be happy if you found me a better house, but...

171
00:10:55,991 --> 00:10:58,227
I'm a shopping pro. Don't worry!

172
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:00,529
Hey, how about this agency?

173
00:11:00,729 --> 00:11:02,531
I often see their ads on TV.

174
00:11:02,731 --> 00:11:05,734
Too naive! Big real estate companies are like department stores.

175
00:11:06,235 --> 00:11:09,972
They have luxury and brand-name goods, but surprisingly little for ordinary folk.

176
00:11:10,172 --> 00:11:12,441
And worst of all, you can't haggle!

177
00:11:12,641 --> 00:11:14,543
I-I didn't know that.

178
00:11:14,843 --> 00:11:20,282
The real find is a small shop tucked away in a corner that's barely hanging on!

179
00:11:23,585 --> 00:11:24,587
Like that one!

180
00:11:27,856 --> 00:11:29,258
"HONEST REAL ESTATE"

181
00:11:29,458 --> 00:11:30,292
W-What?

182
00:11:30,492 --> 00:11:33,028
That's where you find the real bargains.

183
00:11:33,262 --> 00:11:34,129
Let's go, Terai.

184
00:11:34,330 --> 00:11:35,197
Uh, yeah...

185
00:11:35,631 --> 00:11:40,035
What do you mean we only have one contract this month, huh?

186
00:11:40,469 --> 00:11:42,338
But we don't have any good properties...

187
00:11:42,571 --> 00:11:45,274
That's where sales skills come in!

188
00:11:45,874 --> 00:11:47,343
Business is all about strategy!

189
00:11:47,576 --> 00:11:50,512
It's about persuading customers right on the edge of the law.

190
00:11:50,879 --> 00:11:53,449
Chief, we have customers.

191
00:11:58,053 --> 00:11:59,655
All right, leave them to me!

192
00:11:59,855 --> 00:12:02,024
I'll make them sign the contract no matter what.

193
00:12:02,224 --> 00:12:04,293
Smile, smile!

194
00:12:06,962 --> 00:12:07,997
Welcome.

195
00:12:08,597 --> 00:12:13,969
Honest Real Estate will meet all customers' needs with honesty.

196
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:27,216
"HONEST REAL ESTATE"

197
00:12:27,816 --> 00:12:30,386
My name is Tochiro Hanyu. I've been working here honestly

198
00:12:30,619 --> 00:12:34,023
for 40 years as the sales manager at this agency.

199
00:12:34,823 --> 00:12:37,793
What kind of property are you looking for? What's your budget?

200
00:12:38,494 --> 00:12:40,562
About two and a half hours from Tokyo,

201
00:12:40,796 --> 00:12:43,232
I'm looking for a house around 25 million yen.

202
00:12:43,932 --> 00:12:47,503
So he's the one buying? Looks like an easy catch...

203
00:12:48,537 --> 00:12:49,371
In that case...

204
00:12:49,571 --> 00:12:50,572
Wait!

205
00:12:51,006 --> 00:12:53,042
That won't impress the chief.

206
00:12:53,242 --> 00:12:55,811
One hour from Tokyo, with a budget of 15 million!

207
00:12:56,245 --> 00:12:57,813
Hmph! What a demanding guy!

208
00:12:58,013 --> 00:13:01,350
Sir, you're incredibly lucky!

209
00:13:01,550 --> 00:13:05,821
There's a newly completed property that hasn't even been advertised yet!

210
00:13:06,255 --> 00:13:09,591
Just one hour from Tokyo, and the price is only three million yen!

211
00:13:10,025 --> 00:13:11,226
Only that much?!

212
00:13:11,427 --> 00:13:13,228
This is the result of pursuing honesty.

213
00:13:13,429 --> 00:13:15,931
No other agency could ever match this.

214
00:13:16,131 --> 00:13:18,534
This is definitely better than Chief Ohara's house.

215
00:13:18,734 --> 00:13:20,536
It's a real bargain!

216
00:13:21,103 --> 00:13:23,705
Please sign the contract here.

217
00:13:24,073 --> 00:13:25,274
Y-Yes...

218
00:13:26,375 --> 00:13:27,876
Got him.

219
00:13:28,277 --> 00:13:29,545
Wait a minute!

220
00:13:29,945 --> 00:13:31,213
What's wrong, Ryo-san?

221
00:13:31,413 --> 00:13:32,848
From my experience,

222
00:13:33,048 --> 00:13:36,685
no store ever offers the best item to a first-time customer right away!

223
00:13:36,885 --> 00:13:39,788
There must be even better properties!

224
00:13:39,988 --> 00:13:40,989
Gulp!

225
00:13:41,223 --> 00:13:42,624
What are you saying?

226
00:13:42,858 --> 00:13:46,261
We always offer the best property, even to first-time customers.

227
00:13:46,462 --> 00:13:48,464
That's why we're so honest.

228
00:13:48,697 --> 00:13:52,234
That's right. It's rare to find a property this cheap!

229
00:13:52,434 --> 00:13:54,870
It's good we found a better house than the chief did.

230
00:13:55,070 --> 00:13:57,973
Hmm. But I don't like buying it at face value.

231
00:13:58,173 --> 00:13:59,708
There may be room for negotiation.

232
00:14:00,342 --> 00:14:02,311
Uh-oh, this is bad. In that case...

233
00:14:02,544 --> 00:14:04,747
Oh, my cell phone is ringing!

234
00:14:05,547 --> 00:14:07,583
Yes, this is Honesty Real Estate!

235
00:14:08,250 --> 00:14:11,420
Thank you for your patronage.

236
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:13,021
Excuse me for a moment.

237
00:14:14,990 --> 00:14:16,959
Oh? That property?

238
00:14:17,159 --> 00:14:18,460
One moment, please.

239
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:19,661
Oh no!

240
00:14:19,895 --> 00:14:22,297
This caller says he wants to buy that property now!

241
00:14:22,498 --> 00:14:23,332
What?!

242
00:14:23,565 --> 00:14:24,466
What will you do?

243
00:14:24,666 --> 00:14:26,368
If you don't like it,

244
00:14:26,602 --> 00:14:29,338
we'll make a contract with this customer right away...

245
00:14:29,571 --> 00:14:31,340
Okay, I'll sign now!

246
00:14:31,573 --> 00:14:32,775
Ryo-san, give it back!

247
00:14:32,975 --> 00:14:34,510
Deal closed.

248
00:14:35,144 --> 00:14:38,647
I'm terribly sorry, but it's just been sold.

249
00:14:38,847 --> 00:14:41,683
Yes, I'm very sorry.

250
00:14:41,917 --> 00:14:43,018
Excuse me.

251
00:14:43,218 --> 00:14:44,286
Yes, what is it?

252
00:14:44,486 --> 00:14:45,988
Looks like the pen ran out of ink.

253
00:14:46,188 --> 00:14:47,022
What?!

254
00:14:49,057 --> 00:14:50,292
I-I'm sorry!

255
00:14:50,492 --> 00:14:51,326
Hey, Tsukamoto-kun!

256
00:14:51,527 --> 00:14:53,362
Give me a pen! A pen!

257
00:14:53,595 --> 00:14:54,463
Y-Yes.

258
00:14:56,665 --> 00:14:59,401
That impatience isn't normal.

259
00:15:00,202 --> 00:15:01,870
Let me see it again!

260
00:15:10,245 --> 00:15:11,547
Here's a pen.

261
00:15:11,780 --> 00:15:13,549
Let's sign quickly! Let's do it!

262
00:15:13,782 --> 00:15:15,984
-3.0 tsubo? -Gulp!

263
00:15:16,185 --> 00:15:17,886
It's 30 tsubo, Ryo-san.

264
00:15:18,086 --> 00:15:20,055
There's no way a house could be that small.

265
00:15:20,255 --> 00:15:21,623
But something's not right.

266
00:15:21,824 --> 00:15:23,792
Hey, what's this dot?

267
00:15:24,159 --> 00:15:27,863
Sometimes documents get stained with ink.

268
00:15:28,363 --> 00:15:30,365
You're thinking too much, Ryo-san.

269
00:15:30,566 --> 00:15:33,535
Just to be sure, what's the area of the plot?

270
00:15:33,735 --> 00:15:35,571
It's as the document says.

271
00:15:36,038 --> 00:15:37,839
I'm asking how many tsubo!

272
00:15:38,273 --> 00:15:40,375
It's as you can see, sir.

273
00:15:40,876 --> 00:15:43,378
So you won't say how many tsubo it is?

274
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:47,583
Ryo-san, you don't have to get so angry.

275
00:15:47,816 --> 00:15:49,051
Don't you realize, Terai?

276
00:15:49,251 --> 00:15:52,120
He never said 30 tsubo himself!

277
00:15:52,354 --> 00:15:54,122
-Oh, you're right! -Yikes!

278
00:15:54,823 --> 00:15:56,992
That's suspicious.

279
00:15:59,094 --> 00:16:02,297
If you won't say how many tsubo it is, let us see it!

280
00:16:03,065 --> 00:16:05,601
If you hesitate, someone else will take it.

281
00:16:05,834 --> 00:16:07,936
Cut the excuses and just take us there now!

282
00:16:08,570 --> 00:16:09,438
Y-Yes, sir!

283
00:16:14,943 --> 00:16:19,081
Look at this wonderful location and beautiful exterior!

284
00:16:19,281 --> 00:16:23,752
You won't find a better bargain anywhere in the metropolitan area!

285
00:16:24,219 --> 00:16:26,221
And how do people live in it?

286
00:16:26,421 --> 00:16:28,257
Do you shoot them with a shrinking ray?

287
00:16:28,457 --> 00:16:30,592
It really was 3.0 tsubo.

288
00:16:30,792 --> 00:16:32,761
That was close. I almost got tricked!

289
00:16:33,161 --> 00:16:34,763
That's not true.

290
00:16:35,430 --> 00:16:36,965
I had no intention of deceiving you.

291
00:16:37,699 --> 00:16:40,302
How dare you show us a toy house!

292
00:16:40,502 --> 00:16:43,572
I never said it was a human house.

293
00:16:43,772 --> 00:16:45,140
This is a pet house.

294
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:46,241
A pet house?!

295
00:16:50,579 --> 00:16:55,751
More and more pet lovers these days are tired of the same old kennels,

296
00:16:55,951 --> 00:16:59,621
and want high-end pet houses like this one.

297
00:17:00,489 --> 00:17:01,957
It seems extremely suspicious.

298
00:17:02,157 --> 00:17:04,493
Eh? When I first saw you,

299
00:17:04,726 --> 00:17:07,829
I thought you were a pet lover.

300
00:17:08,497 --> 00:17:11,300
I am really, really sorry!

301
00:17:11,833 --> 00:17:14,469
As an apology, I'd like to offer you a great property nearby,

302
00:17:14,670 --> 00:17:18,940
at an honest price of 50% off!

303
00:17:19,141 --> 00:17:21,543
Please accept my apology!

304
00:17:21,777 --> 00:17:23,378
Let's see the actual property first.

305
00:17:23,612 --> 00:17:24,313
Yes, sir!

306
00:17:24,846 --> 00:17:26,081
I won't lose him now.

307
00:17:26,281 --> 00:17:28,450
Next time, I'll make him sign for sure!

308
00:17:36,625 --> 00:17:39,027
Look! That's the house!

309
00:17:39,795 --> 00:17:42,464
It's a pretty nice house. How much is it?

310
00:17:42,664 --> 00:17:44,766
It's supposed to be nearly 20 million yen,

311
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:48,036
but the honest price is just 8.5 million yen!

312
00:17:48,503 --> 00:17:49,871
What? Really?

313
00:17:50,105 --> 00:17:54,176
To be honest, offering at such a low price would put the company in deep red.

314
00:17:54,376 --> 00:17:55,210
But!

315
00:17:58,013 --> 00:18:01,316
The company's motto is honesty! My motto is honesty too!

316
00:18:01,516 --> 00:18:03,552
Honesty is truth, and truth is honesty!

317
00:18:03,785 --> 00:18:07,022
If staying honest means a little red ink, then I accept it!

318
00:18:07,222 --> 00:18:09,324
Long live honesty!

319
00:18:10,025 --> 00:18:13,528
Before other customers find out, let's sign the contract here. Quick!

320
00:18:13,729 --> 00:18:14,563
Y-Yeah.

321
00:18:15,130 --> 00:18:16,398
Gotcha!

322
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:19,835
W-What are you doing?

323
00:18:20,035 --> 00:18:21,670
Let's get a closer look.

324
00:18:21,870 --> 00:18:24,239
No! That's not good! Not good at all! Stop, stop!

325
00:18:24,439 --> 00:18:27,509
What's not good? Are you hiding something again?

326
00:18:27,709 --> 00:18:29,978
Gulp! Anyway, it's not good!

327
00:18:42,157 --> 00:18:43,091
What's this?!

328
00:18:47,529 --> 00:18:49,698
Why you...! I knew it'd be uninhabitable!

329
00:18:49,898 --> 00:18:51,066
N-No way!

330
00:18:51,266 --> 00:18:52,868
You can actually live here!

331
00:18:54,636 --> 00:18:58,306
It has a living room, Japanese-style room, kitchen, and bathroom.

332
00:18:58,907 --> 00:19:00,475
It's like a house for an eel.

333
00:19:00,709 --> 00:19:03,478
So will a family of four sleep head-to-toe?

334
00:19:04,479 --> 00:19:05,614
I can't move!

335
00:19:05,847 --> 00:19:09,284
We'll have to adjust our body sizes to the house with this.

336
00:19:10,085 --> 00:19:11,653
Spacious large bathroom, right?

337
00:19:11,887 --> 00:19:15,257
But you have to go through the bathtub to get to the next room!

338
00:19:15,457 --> 00:19:17,058
That's enough!

339
00:19:19,494 --> 00:19:20,796
Don't worry.

340
00:19:21,029 --> 00:19:23,732
We have many honest properties.

341
00:19:23,932 --> 00:19:26,067
I'm sure we'll have something you like.

342
00:19:26,735 --> 00:19:30,739
Hmph! They're a tough bunch, but next time...

343
00:19:30,939 --> 00:19:34,309
What do you think? Look at this spacious entrance!

344
00:19:34,976 --> 00:19:38,280
This is the dining kitchen, designed with functional beauty.

345
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:41,516
This is the bathroom.

346
00:19:41,750 --> 00:19:44,486
How do you like this bright Japanese-style room!

347
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:48,290
This house comes at an honest price of 15 million yen!

348
00:19:48,490 --> 00:19:50,492
That's an incredible price for the city center.

349
00:19:51,159 --> 00:19:54,596
This is comparable to the chief's house, Ryo-san.

350
00:19:54,796 --> 00:19:55,764
Hmm...

351
00:19:55,964 --> 00:19:56,998
Is it an earthquake?

352
00:19:58,467 --> 00:20:01,770
Hey! Don't close the shutter in an earthquake! Open it now!

353
00:20:01,970 --> 00:20:03,105
What? Open it?

354
00:20:03,305 --> 00:20:04,539
Move! I'll open it!

355
00:20:04,773 --> 00:20:06,308
No, I'll open it!

356
00:20:06,508 --> 00:20:08,009
You jerk! You're in my way!

357
00:20:08,243 --> 00:20:09,511
W-Wait a minute!

358
00:20:10,078 --> 00:20:12,314
So you're hiding something again?

359
00:20:12,514 --> 00:20:13,982
It's just your imagination!

360
00:20:14,316 --> 00:20:16,718
Eh, I'll force it open!

361
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:19,621
Ryo-san!

362
00:20:28,163 --> 00:20:30,398
This house is floating in the sea!

363
00:20:30,632 --> 00:20:32,801
The price is lower because there's no land cost.

364
00:20:33,001 --> 00:20:34,402
It's quite stylish, isn't it?

365
00:20:34,636 --> 00:20:36,872
One typhoon and it's done for!

366
00:20:37,105 --> 00:20:39,107
The next property is definitely fine!

367
00:20:39,307 --> 00:20:42,978
This one is also cheaper because there's no land cost.

368
00:20:43,178 --> 00:20:45,547
There's no way they can live here!

369
00:20:46,114 --> 00:20:48,316
I'm starting to feel sick...

370
00:20:49,117 --> 00:20:50,852
Please build it yourself.

371
00:20:51,052 --> 00:20:53,121
It's pretty cheap with no labor cost.

372
00:20:53,321 --> 00:20:54,523
Listen, you...

373
00:20:56,758 --> 00:20:58,760
Ryo-san, let's give up now.

374
00:20:58,994 --> 00:21:02,397
It's not that easy to find a better house than the chief's.

375
00:21:02,597 --> 00:21:04,699
If we give up, I'll lose!

376
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:07,135
I won't let the chief push me around anymore!

377
00:21:07,335 --> 00:21:10,505
Hey! At this point, I'll turn a blind eye to small things.

378
00:21:10,705 --> 00:21:12,240
Find a better house than this!

379
00:21:13,141 --> 00:21:15,210
Will you really turn a blind eye to small things?

380
00:21:15,410 --> 00:21:16,411
Yeah!

381
00:21:16,611 --> 00:21:19,314
Then, leave it all to me!

382
00:21:36,331 --> 00:21:38,233
This is our secret property!

383
00:21:38,433 --> 00:21:41,369
There's no better house in the Tokyo area.

384
00:21:41,770 --> 00:21:42,938
Good for you, Terai.

385
00:21:43,171 --> 00:21:45,340
It's a much better house than the chief's.

386
00:21:45,540 --> 00:21:48,376
Y-Yes... It doesn't get much sunlight, but...

387
00:21:48,577 --> 00:21:50,111
Not much?!

388
00:21:50,345 --> 00:21:52,214
It gets no sunlight at all!

389
00:21:52,414 --> 00:21:55,550
Why is the house underground anyway?

390
00:21:57,652 --> 00:21:59,454
That's because there's no land cost!

391
00:21:59,654 --> 00:22:02,657
Except for sunlight, this house is better than yours!

392
00:22:02,891 --> 00:22:04,726
That's not the point!

393
00:22:04,926 --> 00:22:07,429
Besides, this place is convenient for commuting!

394
00:22:10,799 --> 00:22:12,133
Only one second to the station!

395
00:22:12,367 --> 00:22:16,137
And it's connected to the platform, so you don't have to pay for the train.

396
00:22:18,139 --> 00:22:22,644
Plus, you can hook up the gas, water, electricity, phone and sewage for free!

397
00:22:22,844 --> 00:22:24,579
That would be illegal!

398
00:22:24,779 --> 00:22:27,215
Even if it's illegal, it's better than your house!

399
00:22:27,582 --> 00:22:31,086
Why you...! You call yourself a cop?!

400
00:22:31,286 --> 00:22:33,688
Chief, don't try to weasel out of it like that.

401
00:22:33,922 --> 00:22:36,658
Why not just admit you lost to me?

402
00:22:36,858 --> 00:22:39,327
I'll beat that rotten attitude out of you!

403
00:22:45,834 --> 00:22:48,270
Excuse me, what about the contract?

404
00:22:48,470 --> 00:22:49,838
Now's not the time for that!

405
00:22:52,540 --> 00:22:53,408
What's this smell?

406
00:22:55,176 --> 00:22:56,945
Chief, it's fine.

407
00:22:57,145 --> 00:22:58,980
I actually like it here!

408
00:22:59,180 --> 00:23:00,548
What? Really?

409
00:23:00,782 --> 00:23:05,520
Yes. Come on, Ryo-san, Chief, let's stop fighting and have some tea.

410
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:07,288
I'll make it right now.

411
00:23:23,872 --> 00:23:25,540
Hey, Ryotsu!

412
00:23:29,878 --> 00:23:32,714
I knew you couldn't find a house!

413
00:23:32,914 --> 00:23:35,984
It was a better house than yours at least!

414
00:23:36,384 --> 00:23:38,386
It seems you were satisfied,

415
00:23:38,586 --> 00:23:41,156
so please sign the contract.

416
00:23:41,356 --> 00:23:44,125
B-But the house has already been destroyed!

417
00:23:44,326 --> 00:23:47,762
No, no, you still said you liked it earlier.

418
00:23:47,996 --> 00:23:48,997
But...

419
00:23:49,197 --> 00:23:51,566
Come on, sign it! Come on, come on!

420
00:23:51,766 --> 00:23:53,034
Give me a break!

421
00:23:53,234 --> 00:23:54,402
Wait!

422
00:23:54,602 --> 00:23:57,505
I'm done with buying houses!

423
00:23:57,706 --> 00:24:00,608
Don't say that. Just sign it!

424
00:24:03,144 --> 00:24:08,917
HYPER-SCHOOLKID VS. RYOTSU
